# Beside compose.yaml as `.env`, which compose reads on every command. docs/operating.md § Docker.

# Every file compose should merge, so a plain `docker compose up -d` gets all of them. Without this
# line, a box that needs compose.gpu.yaml drops it the first time somebody forgets the `-f` flags, and
# the server comes back with no card. Add compose.gpu.yaml for an NVIDIA GPU, and compose.lan.yaml
# to publish both ports on every interface, after reading what it says.
COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml

# The image tag. The minor line takes every patch release on `docker compose pull` and stops at the
# next minor. A release, such as 0.1.24, pins exactly, and has to be changed before each upgrade.
RHAPSODE_VERSION=0.1

# The ports on 127.0.0.1, the uid the server runs as (99:100 on unraid), and pip's trusted hosts for
# a network that intercepts TLS. compose.yaml says what each one is for.
# RHAPSODE_API_PORT=8080
# RHAPSODE_WEB_PORT=8081
# PUID=10001
# PGID=10001
# RHAPSODE_PIP_TRUSTED_HOSTS=
